<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="body-armor">Body Armor for Warlock DPS in Pre-Raid</h2>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="head">Head</h3>Getting sufficiently enough hit rating will be the main challenge in pre-raid gear. The reason for this is the limited amount of stats on lower item-lever gear. <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/skill=202/engineering">
<img alt="Engineering" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Engineering</span></a> provides the best option in the form of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=59449/lightweight-bio-optic-killshades">
<img alt="Lightweight Bio-Optic Killshades" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gizmo_newgoggles.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightweight Bio-Optic Killshades</span></a> in which we can choose which secondary stat we get through Cogwheels. Ideally, we would put in <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=59493/rigid-cogwheel">
<img alt="Rigid Cogwheel" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enggizmos_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rigid Cogwheel</span></a> for the massive amount of hit rating that it provides. <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=57871/helm-of-the-typhonic-beast">
<img alt="Helm of the Typhonic Beast" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_robe_dungeonrobe_c_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Helm of the Typhonic Beast</span></a> is the best option for those who do not have <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/skill=202/engineering">
<img alt="Engineering" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Engineering</span></a>. It has a solid amount of hit rating along with Mastery, it drops from <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=39732/setesh">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Setesh</span></a> in <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=4945/halls-of-origination">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Halls of Origination</span></a>. A less RNG-dependent method would be to spend your <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=395/justice-points">
<span>
<img alt="Justice Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-justice.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Justice Points</span></span></a> on <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=58155/cowl-of-pleasant-gloom">
<img alt="Cowl of Pleasant Gloom" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helm_robe_dungeonrobe_c_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cowl of Pleasant Gloom</span></a>, note that you might want to reforge the critical strike rating to mastery or haste.<div class="box" data-level="null">
<b>Head Enchant</b>: <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=86932/arcanum-of-hyjal">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_masterofelements.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Arcanum of Hyjal</span></a></div>
